    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0138_096c0524f274.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 109px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;1st reaction Markovnikov&#39;s&nbsp;addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;on double bond while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">2</mi><mrow><mi>nd</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> reaction is halide substitution by&nbsp;Finkelstein reaction.</p><p>Finkelstein reaction: An S<sub>N</sub>2 reaction in which one halogen atom (the leaving group) is replaced by iodide&nbsp;(the nucleophile).</p>"
